      "side": 1,
      "message": "Applied the diff and modified a bit. PTAL\n\nSome Recap:\n- [CL 20](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/274934/20): Reuse most existing logic (mReadbackSlots, mDeferredExpectations, detail::Expectation(either clone or shared_ptr)) for the replayed part; Compare the replayed readback buffer using expectation; Most instrusive change to existing logic and scattered around.\n- [CL 28](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/274934/28): Reuse only mReadbackSlots for buffer mapping; Compare the replayed readback buffer with the original test readback buffer; Simpler;\n- [CL 35](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/274934/35): Didn\u0027t reuse existing test logic. Map and unmap manually of the replayed readback buffer and compare with the orignal test readback buffer, after all original test check are done; Simple logic and least intrusive change.\n  - Capture includes the buffer.MapAsync (MapSlotsSynchronously). But current capture logic is no-op for buffer.MapAsync (only captures at buffer.Unmap). So this should be fine.\n  - It maps replayed readbuffer synchronously, compared to the mReadbackSlots map all at once. But we are on webgpu-on-webgpu and capture-replay so we don\u0027t care perf that much.\n   \n   \nFYI on local runs at a glance most failures are due to unimplemented path/validation error/uninteresting mock. AFAICT there\u0027s ~5 that actually fail because of the readback buffer unmatch (maybe the root cause is also the previous ones though).\n\nCL 28 and CL 35 have the similiar ~580 failures out of ~4600 tests.",
